From 50763a2ae3b62645de72850edad2656e55265952 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elliotttate <elliotttate@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 18:16:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 126/128] Smooth Motion: colours blended in the in-between
 frames

The in-between frame blended each draw's matrices and drew it in this
frame's colours: a model fading in or out, a particle's colour over its
life, a flash, the wind's streaks fading, all changed only at 30 FPS. Now
the colours blend too, rounded to the nearest:

- the vertex block's light colours and material and ambient registers
  (in blend(), with the matrices);
- a TEV draw's pixel constants: the TEV colour and konst registers and the
  fog colour. Each matched draw keeps its pixel constants with its record
  (a run of identical ones once), and when its counterpart's colours differ,
  blend_draw makes a block per step (blended_pixel()). The helper thread
  stages it beside the vertex blocks (InterpRanges::pixel), and render()
  binds it as group 2 per part, a batch drawn part by part where the
  parts' blocks differ. The pixel constants travel with the helper's job
  only where they differ from the job before's, as the vertex constants do.
  The alpha-test references and the rest stay this frame's.

Checked on the i9 (BlueWake, Smooth Motion 60, paced, game frames 880-910
of the Outset route): every real frame identical to the build before (31
of 31); every in-between frame differs, in 3,000-4,000 pixels by up to 41
of 255 - the wind's streaks in the sky, which fade, now halfway. On four
E-cores, old and new interleaved, two runs each: game-thread CPU per game
frame 24.1 and 23.7 ms before, 24.9 and 23.3 ms after; GX worker 61/57 and
62/56 percent of a core, the Smooth Motion helper and the render worker the
same. frame_interp_test has the colours: konst 0 to 200 and alpha 255 to 0
blend to 100 and 128, a TEV register -100 to 101 to 1, the material alpha
and a light's colour halfway, and nothing when the colours did not change.
